The Nautilus DevOps team needs to set up CloudWatch logging for their application. They need to create a CloudWatch log group and log stream with the following specifications:

1) The log group name should be xfusion-log-group.

2) The log stream name should be xfusion-log-stream.

Use Terraform to create the CloudWatch log group and log stream. The Terraform working directory is /home/bob/terraform. 
Create the main.tf file (do not create a different .tf file) to accomplish this task.

Note: Right-click under the EXPLORER section in VS Code and select Open in Integrated Terminal to launch the terminal.

SOLUTION
Here is your /home/bob/terraform/main.tf for the CloudWatch log group and log stream:

hcl
resource "aws_cloudwatch_log_group" "xfusion_log_group" {
  name = "xfusion-log-group"
}

resource "aws_cloudwatch_log_stream" "xfusion_log_stream" {
  name           = "xfusion-log-stream"
  log_group_name = aws_cloudwatch_log_group.xfusion_log_group.name
}
💡 Key Details
Log Group: aws_cloudwatch_log_group with name xfusion-log-group.

Log Stream: aws_cloudwatch_log_stream with name xfusion-log-stream.

Dependency: The log stream references the log group's name via aws_cloudwatch_log_group.xfusion_log_group.name, so Terraform creates the group first, then the stream.

Region: Handled by your existing provider.tf (us-east-1).

No tags: Avoid adding a tags block to keep terraform plan clean in LocalStack.

🚀 Execution Steps
bash
cd /home/bob/terraform
terraform init
terraform apply --auto-approve
✅ Confirm No Changes
bash
terraform plan
It should return:

text
No changes. Your infrastructure matches the configuration.
🔍 Verify (optional)
bash
aws --endpoint-url=http://aws:4566 logs describe-log-groups --log-group-name-prefix xfusion-log-group
aws --endpoint-url=http://aws:4566 logs describe-log-streams --log-group-name xfusion-log-group
You should see the log group xfusion-log-group and the log stream xfusion-log-stream listed.

